{
  "reason": "Tier 2: add a jointly trained last-item residual pathway to the existing GRU representation. The trajectory peaked at 0.5400; larger negative pools and the latest BPR-max replacement failed to improve it, while projected attention helped its immediate predecessor. This motivates testing whether preserving the current item's identity through recurrent compression improves next-item ranking, although the observed scores do not establish compression as the cause.",
  "module": [
    "model_design",
    "training_evaluation"
  ],
  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": null,
    "model_design": "Add one gated item-embedding residual inside GRURec, a Tier 2 representation change that lets immediate purchase identity reach the prediction features directly. Define local_projection = nn.Linear(dim, dim, bias=False) and local_gate = nn.Linear(2 * dim, dim), initialize local_gate weights to zero and its bias to -2, and after the existing attention fusion compute local = local_projection(self.embedding(seq)), gate = sigmoid(local_gate(cat([features, local], dim=-1))), then features = features + gate * local before the existing normalization, output dropout, and output projection. Explicitly zero local at padding positions; all new parameters train jointly with the existing network through the unchanged ranking_loss(model, seq, target), yielding one model rather than an auxiliary scorer. Preserve GRURec's constructor and public methods, existing variable names, projected causal attention, tied embeddings, item bias, current BPR-max objective, NEGATIVES=1024, masking, and all training hyperparameters so the residual pathway is the only experimental change.",
    "training_evaluation": "Update write_predict_script() through its existing inspect.getsource(GRURec) export so working/predict.py includes the new residual layers and strictly reconstructs the saved architecture, preserving predict(user_id, history, candidates, *, dataset_name=None). Keep validation and inference history truncation, right padding, and model scoring identical, and preserve checkpoint selection by HR@10 with the existing NDCG@10 tie-break. Retain all four categories, DATA_DIR=os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], supplied preprocessing-seed-0 splits, training seed 42, evaluation seed 42, environment-controlled SASREC_EPOCHS default 200, existing runtime limits, and trial-local artifacts. Train one fresh network per category on one GPU and load exactly one selected checkpoint per route; assess the atomic change using the pinned host macro validation HR@10, without hidden-test access, checkpoint reuse, averaging, or independently fitted scorers."
  }
}
